      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the baseball league, we need to consider the following:\n\n1. **Number of Teams**: There are 9 teams in the league.\n2. **Games per Pair of Teams**: Each pair of teams plays exactly 3 games.\n\nFirst, we calculate the number of unique pairs of teams. The number of ways to choose 2 teams out of 9 is given by the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} \\), where \\( n \\) is the total number of teams and \\( k \\) is the number of teams to choose at a time. Here, \\( n = 9 \\) and \\( k = 2 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9!}{2!(9-2)!} = \\frac{9!}{2! \\cdot 7!}\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the factorials, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{9}{2} = \\frac{9 \\times 8 \\times 7!}{2 \\times 1 \\times 7!} = \\frac{9 \\times 8}{2 \\times 1} = \\frac{72}{2} = 36\n\\]\n\nSo, there are 36 unique pairs of teams.\n\nNext, we need to find out how many games are played in total. Since each pair of teams plays 3 games, we multiply the number of unique pairs by the number of games per pair:\n\n\\[\n36 \\text{ pairs} \\times 3 \\text{ games per pair} = 108 \\text{ games}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played in the season is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{108}\n\\]",
